   "answer": "A Current Profile “specifies the Core outcomes that an organization is currently achieving (or attempting to achieve) and characterizes how or to what extent each outcome is being achieved”【2】.  \nA Target Profile “specifies the desired outcomes that an organization has selected and prioritized for achieving its cybersecurity risk management objectives” and reflects anticipated changes such as new requirements, technology, or threat trends【2】.  \n\nThus, the Current Profile describes the organization’s present state, while the Target Profile describes the desired future state.",
