   "answer": "- GOVERN (GV) – establishes, communicates, and monitors the organization’s cybersecurity risk management strategy, expectations, and policy【6】  \n- IDENTIFY (ID) – categorizes assets and related cybersecurity risks【8】  \n- PROTECT (PR) – safeguards assets to prevent or lower the likelihood and impact of adverse cybersecurity events【1】  \n- DETECT (DE) – finds and analyzes possible cybersecurity attacks and compromises【3】  \n- RESPOND (RS) – takes actions regarding a detected cybersecurity incident, including containment, analysis, mitigation, reporting, and communication【5】  \n- RECOVER (RC) – restores assets and operations affected by a cybersecurity incident and supports timely restoration of normal operations【5】",
