   "answer": "- Tier 1: Partial – an ad‑hoc, informal approach to managing cybersecurity risk, with limited awareness and prioritization not formally based on objectives or threat environment【3†L1-L4】  \n- Tier 2: Risk Informed – risk‑management practices are approved by management but not yet organization‑wide policy; prioritization is directly informed by risk objectives, threat environment, or business/mission requirements【7†L2-L5】  \n- Tier 3: Repeatable – risk‑management practices are formally approved as policy, regularly updated, and applied organization‑wide; consistent methods and shared information support effective response to changes【6†L1-L5】  \n- Tier 4: Adaptive – an agile, risk‑informed approach that continuously improves and adapts to changing threats and business needs (described as the highest tier in the framework)【1†L1-L3】",
