   "answer": "1. Scope the Organizational Profile – document the high‑level facts and assumptions that define its scope; an organization may have multiple profiles with different scopes (e.g., whole organization, specific systems, or threat‑specific)【4】.  \n2. Gather the information needed to prepare the Organizational Profile – collect policies, risk‑management priorities, resources, enterprise risk profiles, business impact analysis registers, cybersecurity requirements and standards, practices, tools, and work‑role information【3】【4】.  \n3. Create the Organizational Profile – decide what information the profile should include for the selected CSF outcomes, document that information, and consider the risk implications of the Current Profile to inform Target Profile planning and prioritization; also consider using a Community Profile as the basis for the Target Profile【3】.",
